From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 11:37:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: cover emulated border colours in the Meson suite

The custom border emulation reconstructs a Vulkan border colour from two
Metal samples, and a depth-compare sample additionally reconstructs the
comparison against that border.  Pin both shapes and the comparison
contract they rely on: a sampler compare operation is a three-bit mask of
the orderings that pass, and every non-constant operation has a reference
value that the 0.0 and 1.0 Metal borders answer differently, which is what
lets two probes recover the border's filter weight.

The KosmicKrisp Meson suite only exists from "implement GPU geometry
shaders and streams" onward, so the coverage lands here rather than in the
border-colour topic itself.

(cherry picked from commit 037fef4a0161344cb62a15bf9a44aaecb4cd9d64)
(cherry picked from commit 9e2d7bb793a7c26af266ba749dad2513d8eb7054)
